## What to Build

### schemas.py
Pydantic v2 models:
- SkinProfile: monk_tone (int 1-10), observed_concerns (list[str]), skin_type (str), confirmed_concerns (list[str]), allergies (list[str]), budget_monthly (int), goals (list[str]), fragrance_free (bool)
- ConversationTurn: role (str), content (str)
- AnalysisRequest: image_base64 (str)
- ChatRequest: conversation_history (list[ConversationTurn]), skin_profile (SkinProfile), user_message (str)
- RecommendationResponse: product_name (str), brand (str), amazon_asin (str), routine_step (str), why_recommended (str), key_ingredients (list[str])

---

### vision_service.py
Function: analyze_skin_photo(image_base64: str) -> SkinProfile

Call GPT-4o Vision with the image. System prompt should instruct it to:
- Estimate the Monk Skin Tone (1-10 scale, where 1 is lightest and 10 is deepest)
- Identify visible skin concerns (hyperpigmentation, texture, dryness, oiliness, redness, acne)
- Estimate skin type (oily/dry/combination/normal)
- Return ONLY a JSON object matching the SkinProfile schema (observed_concerns and monk_tone filled, everything else empty defaults)
- Never make medical diagnoses
- If image quality is too low to analyze, return monk_tone: 0 as a signal

Parse the JSON response and return a SkinProfile object.

---

### rag_service.py
On startup, load all .txt files from knowledge_base/products/ and knowledge_base/ingredients/ into an in-memory Chroma collection using OpenAI embeddings (text-embedding-ada-002).

Function: retrieve_relevant_products(skin_profile: SkinProfile, top_k: int = 3) -> list[str]

Build a query string from the skin profile fields (monk tone, concerns, skin type, goals, budget, fragrance preference) and do a semantic similarity search against the Chroma collection. Return the top_k most relevant document chunks as strings.

---

### conversation_service.py
Function: get_next_response(conversation_history: list[ConversationTurn], skin_profile: SkinProfile, user_message: str, retrieved_context: list[str]) -> tuple[str, SkinProfile, bool]

Returns: (assistant_response, updated_skin_profile, is_ready_to_recommend)

System prompt for GPT-4o:
"""
You are SkinSage, a knowledgeable and empathetic AI skincare consultant.

You have already analyzed the user's photo. Their current skin profile is provided to you.

Your job is to have a natural conversation to fill in the missing profile fields. Ask ONE question at a time. Never ask multiple questions in one turn. Keep responses to 2-3 sentences max.

Ask about in this order (skip if already known):
1. Their main skin concern right now
2. Any known allergies or sensitivities to ingredients
3. Monthly skincare budget in USD
4. Whether they prefer fragrance-free products
5. Any current products they are already using and want to keep

After you have collected at least: confirmed_concerns, budget_monthly, and fragrance_free — set is_ready_to_recommend to true in your response.

When ready to recommend, do not give recommendations in conversation. Just say you have everything you need and will generate their routine now.

Never diagnose medical conditions. Never say a product will definitely work. Always say results may vary and to patch test new products.

Current skin profile from photo analysis:
{skin_profile}

Relevant product and ingredient context from knowledge base:
{retrieved_context}

Update the skin profile JSON with any new information extracted from the user's message. Return your response as JSON:
{{
  "assistant_response": "your conversational response here",
  "updated_profile": {{ ...full updated SkinProfile as JSON... }},
  "is_ready_to_recommend": false
}}
"""

Parse the JSON response and return the tuple.

